ld_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n`master` [30a0296cc25d7d62fd16e6f9ed5977c6c0ec0e3c]\n`v4.8.dev1.official` [ebbf577a0]\nEven `v4.6.stable.official` [89cea1439]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev1 - macOS Sequoia (15.7.5) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M4 (Apple9) - Apple M4 (10 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf this exact issue was already reported, you can close this. Otherwise, I didn't see this exact issue when searching.\n\nWhen manually editing a `NodePath` in the Inspector by clicking on `Edit` and writing something invalid (even an empty value), it shows this error as a toaster notification and in Output. `INTERNAL ERROR: Node not found: \"\" (relative to \"/root/@EditorNode@20410/@Panel@14/@VBoxContainer@16/DockVSplitMain/DockHSplitMain/@VBoxContainer@38/DockVSplitCenter/@VSplitContainer@102/@VBoxContainer@103/@EditorMainScreen@161/MainScreen/@CanvasItemEditor@10250/@VSplitContainer@9931/@HSplitContainer@9933/@HSplitContainer@9935/@Control@9936/@SubViewportContainer@9937/@SubViewport@9938/Node2D\").`\n\nIn `v4.8.dev1` and `v4.6.stable`, it didn't toast anything, but now it is more obvious. I think it should still throw an error because it's still an invalid value, just not the above since it wouldn't make sense to most users since they would expect it to be referring to the tree that they're editing, not the internal `SceneTree`. Except when the value is empty, which I would expect to simply clear the value and not throw any error. This only happens for `Node` variables which are exported to the Inspector, native nodes like `Control` don't show this when assigning focus neighbors an invalid value for example.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nHave a `Node` with a script that exports a `Node` variable. Click on the kebab dropdown and choose `Edit`. Then press Enter (even empty node names error). The error should appear as a toast and/or in the Output.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30304754/MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121678/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121678/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}